Home menu: a centred card over the dimmed game, grouped, in the launcher's words.

From the design critique. The menu was a 640x480 sheet stretched over the
whole window: opaque, so the display settings it changes could not be judged,
and stretched, so the 8x8 font went wide and uneven on a 16:9 or 21:9 window.
Twelve rows had no grouping, names differed from the launcher's for the same
settings, Image fit cycled in a different order, and the armed "press again"
state of Restart/Quit reddened both rows.

psx_pause_menu.c/.h:
- a 420x480 portrait card. Rows in four captioned groups - GAME (Resume,
  Quick save, Quick load), DISPLAY (Gameplay aspect, Image fit, Window mode,
  FPS counter, Post-processing), ASSISTS (Keep 99 lives, Aku Aku), SYSTEM
  (Restart, Quit) - from one row table that drawing and psx_pause_menu_row_at
  share; captions and gaps hit nothing;
- names as in the launcher (GAMEPLAY ASPECT, FPS COUNTER, POST-PROCESSING,
  KEEP 99 LIVES, AKU AKU: OFF / KEEP 2 MASKS / NO DAMAGE); "< value >" arrows
  hug the value; armed red shows on the selected row only;
- a one- or two-line note under the list for the selected row. Gameplay
  aspect and Image fit say they apply when you resume: the held frame behind
  the menu is a capture with the old framing baked in;
- Crash orange (#F07E1E) is the one accent, as in the launcher (5.3:1 on the
  selected row); every text colour is >= 4.5:1 on its background;
- psx_pause_menu_place(): centred on the presenter's surface, at a whole 2x,
  3x... when that fits with a 16 px margin, so glyphs stay square; fitted at
  0.96 of the surface below 2x. PSX_PAUSE_BACKDROP_KEEP (96/255) is how much
  of the frame shows behind it.

gpu_gl_renderer.c (GL and D3D12): gl_dim_frame() multiplies the default
framebuffer by a 1x1 grey through the present program (blend ZERO,SRC_COLOR;
alpha ZERO,ONE), then the panel is drawn at its placed rect. Every hold
capture is taken before gl_swap_with_osd(), so the pause loop's re-presents
never compound the dim. host_osd.c (SDL renderer): a black fill at
255-KEEP alpha, then the panel at its rect on the logical size.

main.cpp: Image fit steps letterbox, fill, fit width, stretch (the
launcher's order); the mode values are unchanged. The mouse is mapped into
the presenter's surface (drawable pixels for GL/D3D12, logical coordinates
for the SDL renderer) and through psx_pause_menu_place().

No file here is in codegen_hash_sources.cmake: no recompile, no cache rebuild.

